null,"context":{"background":[{"title":"Tariff","extract":"A tariff, or import tax, is a duty imposed by a national government, customs territory, or supranational union on imports of goods and is paid by the importer. Exceptionally, an export tax may be levied on exports of goods or raw materials and is paid by the exporter. Besides being a source of revenue, import duties can also be a form of regulation of foreign trade and policy that burden foreign products to encourage or safeguard domestic industry. Protective tariffs are among the most widely used instruments of protectionism, along with import quotas and export quotas and other non-tariff barriers to trade.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tariff","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"places":[{"title":"Iran","extract":"Iran, officially the Islamic Republic of Iran, and historically known as Persia, is a country in West Asia. It borders Iraq to the west; Turkey, Azerbaijan, and Armenia to the northwest; the Caspian Sea to the north, Turkmenistan to the northeast; Afghanistan to the east; Pakistan to the southeast; and the Gulf of Oman and the Persian Gulf to the south. With a population of over 92 million, Iran ranks 17th globally in both geographic size and population. It is divided into five regions with 31 provinces. Tehran is the nation's capital and largest city and serves as its primary economic center.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"IR"}],"arc":{"reports":96,"first_seen":"2026-10-10T03:22:00Z","first_title":"Rebecca Cooke calls for reversing tariffs, ending Iran war during agricultural campaign stops","first_url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","first_publisher":"news8000.com","earlier":[{"id":"e_149431ed079a","title":"Healthcare, Iran war & tariffs: Resurgent Democrats set stage to confront Trump","date":"2026-11-07T13:57:00Z","url":"https://news.google._?oc=5","publisher":"The Times of India","verification":"single_sourc